    <!-- Dzongkha locale is registered (selectable in Settings) but the
    string VALUES below are deliberately left in English rather than
    machine-guessed Dzongkha: administrative/security terminology is exactly
    the kind of vocabulary where a confidently wrong translation is a real
    safety issue, not a cosmetic one, and this build's Dzongkha proficiency
    isn't reliable enough to answer for it. Only the language's own native
    name (རྫོང་ཁ) is used, since that is well-attested. The Settings screen
    shows an explicit "unverified translation" notice on this option — see
    settings_language_label usage in SettingsScreen.kt — and this file
    should be replaced with a native speaker's real translations before
    this locale is presented as genuinely localized. -->
